2 Types of Vertulization 
1. HVM (Hardware Virtual Machine) 
Runs directly on hardware using full virtualization. 
Allows the instance to use hardware features like CPU, network, and storage efficiently. 
Best For: 
• Most modern EC2 instance types 
• High performance 
• Windows instances 
• Linux instances with high CPU/GPU needs 
2. PV (Paravirtualization) (Older method) 
Uses a software layer to communicate with hardware. 
Slower than HVM and mostly phased out. 
Best For: 
• Old Linux kernels 
• Older workloads (not commonly used now) 
